  "id": "COMPOUND:26367 - PROTEIN:5836",
  "verbalization": "CID 127037596 is associated with the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme, which is a key target of multiple complex molecular structures. These structures, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, all share a common target of HUVEC. The evidence suggests that CID 127037596 acts as a modulator of the sialyltransferase enzyme, which is involved in the synthesis of sialic acid, a critical component in cell surface glycosylation. This mechanism implies that the drug may influence cellular processes related to glycosylation, potentially affecting cell function and signaling. The consistent association of CID 127037596 with the sialyltransferase enzyme and its downstream targets, including HUVEC, supports a role in modulating cellular activity through this pathway.",
